-- title:
--   Naturality of level automorphisms on the supersingular charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ (that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$). Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places for $q$, assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ whose residue map is compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$ (`hR₀`). Further data: an index $\zeta$ in the primitive $q$-th roots of unity, valuation subrings $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ indexed by $W$, subject to the Igusa-chart hypotheses (`hIg_inf` describing $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ by Laurent series over $A$, transitivity under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, and permutation of the family by level automorphisms) and the supersingular-chart hypotheses (`hSS_A`, `hSS_over`, invariance `hSS_fix` under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and existence of a transversal element `hSS_tr`); a semistable covering $\mathcal{C}$ for $(q,M',A,W)$; regular prolongations $R_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $R_{\mathrm{SS}}(s).\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ agreeing with the charts $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$ in integers and residues; and disc families $\mathrm{discS}$, $\mathrm{coordS}$ for $R_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ over the complement of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$'s nodes, together with the transport hypothesis `htransS` for semilinear automorphisms fixing $A$, its maximal ideal and the image of $j_q$, the description `hdomS` of the chart domains by discs, the determination `hpmS`, `hpmS_off` of the place map, and the stability `hNstabS`, `hdiscstabS` of the node set and of the discs under the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. The conclusion quantifies over a further index, again written $\zeta$, and over $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $s \in W$: writing $g$ for the semilinear automorphism of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ attached to the algebra automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ (trivial on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), there is an automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{FSS}\,s$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ such that $g$ preserves the integers of the chart $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$ in both directions and its residue map intertwines $g$ with $\varphi$, and such that $(\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s).\mathrm{placeMap}(g \cdot P) = \varphi \cdot (\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s).\mathrm{placeMap}(P)$ for every place $P$ in the chart's domain.
--
--   This is the supersingular half of the naturality statement for the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve: the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ act on each supersingular chart through an automorphism of its reduced function field, compatibly with the chart's place map. It is used in the assembly of the existence theorem for such coverings, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted).
